--TEST--
A string literal at a `property<static>` field of an attribute payload that names no public instance property of the class the attribute is on does not compile: a misspelled name, a `private` property, a `static` property, a wrong name in a list and the comma-separated form are each one diagnostic at the literal — `rule:attributes/a-declaration-names-its-class-with-static`
--FILE--
<?nvs
attribute Search on class { fields: array<property<static>> }
attribute Sort on class { by: property<static> }

#[Sort(by: 'titel')]
class A {
    public string $title = '';
}

#[Sort(by: 'secret')]
class B {
    private string $secret = '';
    public string $title = '';
}

#[Sort(by: 'count')]
class C {
    public static int $count = 0;
    public string $title = '';
}

#[Search(fields: ['title', 'autor'])]
class D {
    public string $title = '';
    public string $author = '';
}

#[Search(fields: ['author, title'])]
class E {
    public string $title = '';
    public string $author = '';
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0405]: `A` has no public property `$titel`
  --> case.nvs:5:12
%Aerror[E0405]: `B` has no public property `$secret`
   --> case.nvs:10:12
%Aerror[E0405]: `C` has no public property `$count`
   --> case.nvs:16:12
%Aerror[E0405]: `D` has no public property `$autor`
   --> case.nvs:22:28
%Aerror[E0405]: `E` has no public property `$author, title`
   --> case.nvs:28:19
%A
